# Seat 0 draws the second 8s, closes 3333m, then discards its replacement 7z
# in riichi. The 24m kanchan needs a fifth 3m, and all four copies are in the kan.
# Both rulesets accept riichi and count Seat 0 as the only tenpai seat at exhaustive draw.
# Seat 0 pays 1000 for riichi and collects the 3000 noten pool (1000 from each opponent).
# Net deltas are +2000, -1000, -1000, -1000. The 1000 stick carries over.
# Seat 3 holds four pairs and five loose tiles (not six pairs: that would be a
# seven-pairs tenpai and a second tenpai seat, as an earlier draft had it).

[meta]
name: riichi_fifth_copy_closed_kan
title: Both rulesets allow riichi on a fifth-copy wait when the four copies form a closed kan
rules: both
source: rules.md §1 riichi_karaten_allowed, §5.7; real-log campaign, docs/notes/p3-reallogs.md

[round]
scores: 25000 25000 25000 25000

[wall]
hand 0: 3333m 24m 234p 567p 8s
hand 1: 147m 147p 147s 2346z
hand 2: 258m 369p 259s 1235z
hand 3: 6699m 1188p 1469s 6z
dora: 1z 2z
rinshan: 7z
draws: 8s

[steps]
0 ankan 3m
assert_legal 0: riichi
0 riichi
0 tsumogiri 7z
auto_tsumogiri 68

